**ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException:**

Occurs when you try to access an **invalid index**.

**Valid vs Invalid Indices:**
```java
int[] arr = {10, 20, 30};  // Length = 3

// VALID indices: 0, 1, 2
System.out.println(arr[0]);  // ✅ OK: 10
System.out.println(arr[2]);  // ✅ OK: 30

// INVALID indices:
System.out.println(arr[3]);   // ❌ ERROR! Index out of bounds
System.out.println(arr[-1]);  // ❌ ERROR! Negative index
```

**Why It Happens:**
- Array of size n has indices **0 to n-1**
- Accessing index >= length → Exception
- Accessing negative index → Exception

