**Array Reversal Algorithm:**

**In-Place Reversal:**
```java
public class ReverseArray {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] numbers = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};

        System.out.print("Original: ");
        printArray(numbers);  // 1 2 3 4 5

        // Reverse: swap from ends toward center
        for (int i = 0; i < numbers.length / 2; i++) {
            int temp = numbers[i];
            numbers[i] = numbers[numbers.length - 1 - i];
            numbers[numbers.length - 1 - i] = temp;
        }

        System.out.print("Reversed: ");
        printArray(numbers);  // 5 4 3 2 1
    }

    public static void printArray(int[] arr) {
        for (int num : arr) {
            System.out.print(num + " ");
        }
        System.out.println();
    }
}
```

**Why Loop to length/2?**

**Visualization:**
```
Array: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
Indices: 0  1  2  3  4

Iteration 1 (i=0):
  Swap: arr[0] ↔ arr[4]
  Result: [5, 2, 3, 4, 1]

Iteration 2 (i=1):
  Swap: arr[1] ↔ arr[3]
  Result: [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]

Iteration 3 (i=2):
  Would swap arr[2] ↔ arr[2] (middle element)
  Not needed!

If i=3 (WRONG!):
  Would swap arr[3] ↔ arr[1]
  Undoes previous swap!
  Result: [5, 2, 3, 4, 1] (broken!)
```

**Loop only halfway:**
```java
// ✅ CORRECT - Stop at middle
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length / 2; i++) {
    // Swap pairs from outside in
}

// ❌ WRONG - Swaps twice, undoing reversal
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    // First half reverses, second half un-reverses!
}
```

**Opposite Index Formula:**
```java
opposite_index = length - 1 - i

For length=5:
  i=0 → opposite = 5-1-0 = 4
  i=1 → opposite = 5-1-1 = 3
  i=2 → opposite = 5-1-2 = 2 (middle)
```

**Two-Pointer Approach:**
```java
public static void reverse(int[] arr) {
    int left = 0;
    int right = arr.length - 1;

    while (left < right) {
        // Swap
        int temp = arr[left];
        arr[left] = arr[right];
        arr[right] = temp;

        // Move pointers
        left++;
        right--;
    }
}
```

**Even vs Odd Length:**
```java
// Odd length: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] → 5/2 = 2 iterations
// Swaps: (0,4), (1,3), middle stays

// Even length: [1, 2, 3, 4] → 4/2 = 2 iterations
// Swaps: (0,3), (1,2), all elements swapped
```

**Time and Space Complexity:**
- **Time:** O(n/2) = O(n)
- **Space:** O(1) - in-place, only temp variable

